{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaIMME","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaIMME","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.imme_third_diff_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.imme_third_diff_zero","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaIMME.lean#L60-L69","doc":"**Askey–Racah / Wigner truncation, made falsifiable.** A degree-2 IMME has a\n**vanishing third finite difference**\n`Δ³f(x) = f(x+3) − 3 f(x+2) + 3 f(x+1) − f(x) = 0`. Equivalently: no `d·T₃³`\nterm can hide in the residual — the \"charge-dependent forces are rank-≤2\nisotensors\" statement (the Askey–Racah cutoff) is the testable identity that a\nfourth multiplet member must satisfy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.imme_triplet_2nd_diff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.imme_triplet_2nd_diff","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaIMME.lean#L52-L58","doc":"**Triplet 2nd difference isolates the quadratic.** For an isobaric triplet\n`T₃ ∈ {−1, 0, +1}`, the symmetric second difference `f(1) + f(−1) − 2·f(0)`\ncancels `a` and `b·T₃`, leaving `2·c`. This is why measuring `c` requires three\nmultiplet members, not a mirror pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.imme_mirror_diff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.imme_mirror_diff","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaIMME.lean#L44-L50","doc":"**Mirror difference isolates the linear coefficient.** The bar-even `a` and\n`c·T₃²` cancel, leaving `2·b·T₃`. This is the explicit-quadratic refinement of\n`mirror_baseline_cancels` (#3089): a mirror pair can only ever measure `b`,\nnever `c`, no matter how large the quadratic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.imme_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.imme_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaIMME.lean#L39-L42","doc":"**The isoscalar.** The central (`T₃ = 0`) value is `a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.imme","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.imme","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaIMME.lean#L35-L37","doc":"The IMME form: a degree-2 polynomial in the isospin projection `T₃`,\n`a + b·T₃ + c·T₃²`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}